NXR-141|Simple application starting surface|Usability|The project shall provide a short application guide and optional convenience header showing copied messages, scoped device transactions and queued printf while preserving existing low-level APIs.|Keep the small RTOS approachable without removing useful optional mechanisms.|One header exposes enabled services without automatic allocation; named event waits avoid positional mode booleans; existing signatures remain valid; a small console example cross-links with a labeled counting sink and explicit board clock replacement; detailed ISR and ownership contracts remain accessible.|Public-header host fixtures, console firmware link/audit, documentation build and future board integration.|NXR-115,NXR-122,NXR-140|RTOS_SYNC and optional RTOS_LOGGING; existing nano remains feature-off.|Convenience includes have no independent runtime storage; example objects and stacks are statically reserved.|include/rtos_ipc.hpp,include/rtos_sync.hpp,examples/console.cpp,docs/simple-start.rst|Simplicity pass supplies a short starting path and compatible named APIs; hardware UART, IRQ, clock and timing qualification remain outstanding.|include/rtos_ipc.hpp,include/rtos_sync.hpp,examples/console.cpp|tests/public_api.cpp|PartialSourceUnverified
